{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/937314-1e-werewolf-character-creation-gift-help","id":937314,"title":"1e werewolf character creation gift help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-25T15:02:36-07:00","id":937314,"title":"1e werewolf character creation gift help","content":"Once a month i get together with my friends for a world of darkness campaign and at the end of our session this month i borrowed the book to make my first werewolf but it seems very complicated to me. i have no idea which gifts i am allowed to pick from to start with.<br /> <br /> Currently i decided on Elodoth Stormlord and put three points towards Honor<br /> <br /> Any advice would be greatly appreciated<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T16:47:36-07:00","id":937371,"title":"","content":"You get 3 gifts. Two of those gifts must be affinity gifts, one each from your Auspice and one from your Tribe. The last gift can be from any Gift list (barring other Auspice specific gifts. Your Elodoth could not take a Rahu's Full Moon gifts, for example.)<br /> <br /> And Elodoth Storm Lord's affinity gifts are these:<br /> <br /> Auspice: <b>Insight, Warding, Half Moon,</b> Honor, Judge's Moon<br /> <br /> Tribe: <b>Weather, Evasion, Alpha, </b>Dominance, Halcyon<br /> <br /> Bolded ones are in the Core Werewolf the Forsaken book.<br /> <br /> Gifts rank from 1-5, as does renown. You start with the first rank and go up. Choose your affinity gifts first, then you can use your third free gift to get the second rank of any of the affinity gifts you've chosen, or the first rank in a gift from any other list (again, barring auspice gifts). That's pretty much it. This is a cliff notes version tailored to your specific character, but later it might be good to remember that you can never have a gift higher than your primary renown (which is in this case, Honor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T05:37:00-07:00","id":937557,"title":"","content":"Also: you cannot have 3 dots in one renown at character creation. It's on page 83. I wouldn't recommend it anyway, because you would have to take all 3 auspice gifts and that is pretty boring for a starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:02:14-07:00","id":937578,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong, but I think you <i>could</i> have 3 dots in one renown in 1st Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:18:55-07:00","id":937614,"title":"","content":"Ah sorry, I had 2e in mind. Yeah don't know about first. I just had a glimps at first edition once right at the time second came out and decide that I should switch to second edition right away. Anyway, sorry for the useless ramblings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:28:28-07:00","id":937668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/937314-1e-werewolf-character-creation-gift-help?p=937578#post937578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be wrong, but I think you <i>could</i> have 3 dots in one renown in 1st Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I've built starting characters with 3 dots in one Renown in 1e games before. But it's been a long time, I can't remember if that was a house rule our group was using or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:43:49-07:00","id":937679,"title":"","content":"P63, 'Your third dot can be allocated to any of the \ufb01ve Renown types as you please. It could go toward primary Renown type, or to another type altogether.'<br /> <br /> Your first two go to your Auspice and Tribal renown, you would likely only be able to get 3 dots in one Renown if you had an Auspice and Tribe with the same Renown, for instance an Irraka Iron Master with Cunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:25:40-07:00","id":938610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/937314-1e-werewolf-character-creation-gift-help?p=937371#post937371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get 3 gifts. Two of those gifts must be affinity gifts, one each from your Auspice and one from your Tribe. The last gift can be from any Gift list (barring other Auspice specific gifts. Your Elodoth could not take a Rahu's Full Moon gifts, for example.)<br /> <br /> And Elodoth Storm Lord's affinity gifts are these:<br /> <br /> Auspice: <b>Insight, Warding, Half Moon,</b> Honor, Judge's Moon<br /> <br /> Tribe: <b>Weather, Evasion, Alpha, </b>Dominance, Halcyon<br /> <br /> Bolded ones are in the Core Werewolf the Forsaken book.<br /> <br /> Gifts rank from 1-5, as does renown. You start with the first rank and go up. Choose your affinity gifts first, then you can use your third free gift to get the second rank of any of the affinity gifts you've chosen, or the first rank in a gift from any other list (again, barring auspice gifts). That's pretty much it. This is a cliff notes version tailored to your specific character, but later it might be good to remember that you can never have a gift higher than your primary renown (which is in this case, Honor).</div> </div> </div> </div>i couldn't find any gifts labeled Alpha but i did find dominance so i'm guessing you mixed the two up.<br /> <br /> So just to make sure basically the gift's i'm not allowed to pick are:<br /> Cresent moon<br /> Death<br /> Elemental<br /> Father wolf's<br /> Full moon<br /> Gibbous moon<br /> inspiration <br /> Knowledge<br /> Mother Luna's<br /> Nature<br /> New moon<br /> Rage<br /> Shaping<br /> Stealth<br /> Strength<br /> Technology<br /> <br /> <br /> and the ones i am allowed to pick from are:<br /> Dominance<br /> Evasion<br /> Half moon<br /> insight<br /> Warding<br /> Weather<br /> <br /> Then when i gain a dot in renown i get another free gift with the same amount of dots like if i gained another dot in honor i would get to pick a 4 dot gift from one of the six from the second list or a 1 dot gift from the second list? Thanks for the responses so far, hopefully i will eventually understand this system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:07:55-07:00","id":938626,"title":"","content":"Alpha Gifts are in The Rage, the Werewolf Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> I do believe you're allowed to pick Father Wolf and Mother Luna Gifts, as well. They are considered Affinity Gifts to all Forsaken.<br /> <br /> If you gain a fourth dot of Honor Renown you get, for free, a four dot Gift in any of your Affinity Gifts, which should be listed on the relevant Tribe or Auspice section, as well as the werewolf template quick reference, on p66 of the core book, though I'm sure Amravanti's list is correct. You might want to double check and just write down which Gifts your character has an Affinity for somewhere on their character sheet.<br /> <br /> If you want a Gift you do not have Affinity for, such as Technology, you need to purchase it with Experience and can't get it as a freebie for gaining Renown. They cost extra Experience, being non-Affinity Gifts.<br /> <br /> Gifts don't need to be learned in order, keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:32:33-07:00","id":939140,"title":"","content":"Ah, I must've accidentally switched around Dominance and Alpha, but yes you have the hang of it. <br /> <br /> If you get your 4th dot of Honor you can get any 4th dot gift from your Affinity lists.<br /> <br /> If you got your 1st dot of Cunning, it'd be any 1st dot gift from your Affinity lists.<br /> <br /> Nofather is also correct that Mother Luna and Father Wolf are affinity gifts for all werewolves. <br /> <br /> You can buy gifts independent from renown, including gifts outside of your Affinity lists (for an increased cost), however they must be bought in ascending order (gifts can be skipped at a cost of three xp per skipped rank)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:42:53-07:00","id":939150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/937314-1e-werewolf-character-creation-gift-help?p=939140#post939140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can buy gifts independent from renown, including gifts outside of your Affinity lists (for an increased cost), however they must be bought in ascending order (gifts can be skipped at a cost of three xp per skipped rank)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm drawing a blank, I've never heard of this tax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:49:02-07:00","id":939157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/937314-1e-werewolf-character-creation-gift-help?p=939150#post939150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm drawing a blank, I've never heard of this tax.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah it was a 1e mechanic I was never much a fan of.<br /> <br /> &quot;Another way to learn Gifts in a list without knowing their predecessors is with experience points. In this case, the experience cost is simply higher than normal. When your character learns a Gift without \ufb01rst learning all those of lower level in the list<b>,<i> the cost to learn the new Gift increases by three experience points per Gift that is skipped.</i></b>Therefore, learning a four-dot Gift from an auspice or tribal af\ufb01nity list without \ufb01rst learning the appropriate two-dot and three-dot Gifts costs 26 experience points instead of the usual 20. Similarly, if a four-dot Gift is learned from a list that\u2019s not af\ufb01liated with auspice or tribe (or that is not from one of the common lists) while skipping the \ufb01rst three Gifts on the list, the Gift costs 37 experience points instead of 28.<br /> <br /> Skipping dots in a Gift list does not allow you to ignore your character\u2019s highest primary Renown trait. If your character\u2019s highest primary Renown is 4, he can\u2019t skip ahead to a \ufb01ve-dot Gift in any list. No Gifts can be skipped at character creation to learn ones of higher level. They must be taken sequentially by starting characters. The Gift lists presented here should not be considered the only ones in existence. These are simply the most common. Storytellers may design their own Gift lists or approve lists designed by players.&quot;<br /> <br /> page 103, Werewolf the Forsaken (1e)<br /> <br /> Edit: Woah, posted way more than I intended to in this quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:56:00-07:00","id":939159,"title":"","content":"I think I just blanked out everything beyond, 'Your character does not have to learn Gifts of a given list sequentially, either.'<br /> <br /> Thank you, Stew Wilson and writers of Werewolf second edition for giving us a much easier time of making sense of the book and getting things within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:31:58-07:00","id":939625,"title":"","content":"it's so weird, for other character types usually stacking three or four dots in one area seems to save EXP spent in the long run but for werewolves it seems to be a better investment to split up the three dots in renown at character creation. This way at least two of the five renown can be bought at x6 instead of x8 per new dot along with the fact you get free gifts per new dot renown.<br /> <br /> Now that i understand the\u200b system a little better maybe i'll start over, right now i'm still going Elodoth but am unsure which tribe i want. Any suggestions, tips, advice, or correction help with rules i misunderstood would be much appreciated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:57:31-07:00","id":939688,"title":"","content":"It fits for Werewolf. Gifts aren't just magic powers werewolves get, when they're given to you by a spirit, the spirit changes your very soul, and even your Essence changes subtly. You become more focused, like a spirit, towards one thing. Branching out from there can be difficult, at least to start.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the Gifts in first edition were really messy, and find second edition's take on it much better. Not just with Experience costs, but also overall 'power level.' The first edition gifts varied strangely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:19:24-07:00","id":940798,"title":"","content":"The free specialty in investigation seemed appealing to me at first but aside from that i don't really care for the half moon gifts so i decided against Elodoth. At the moment i'm pretty sure i want to go Storm Lord but have no idea which Auspice to start out as.<br /> <br /> Anyone want to suggest a solid 1e starter build, or give me another persons insight on the matter, or even any advice on the subject at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:38:55-07:00","id":940922,"title":"","content":"Before second edition, I always preferred Ithaeur.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the Half-Moon Gifts, you might look at the Judge's Moon Gifts, also Elodoth Auspice from the book Lore of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I'd normally think of my character first then pick their powers from what's available, so perhaps I'm not able to offer the best advice for this. What kind of powers do you want for your character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:30:58-07:00","id":941698,"title":"","content":"Next month our usual story teller is going to be on his honeymoon and our replacement GM likes to make us engage in combat. i usually like to make characters that use less EXP to improve by stacking 4 dots where ever possible in terms of attributes/merits/skills and try to be as useful as i can outside of combat, because to me it's the least interesting part of the game.<br /> <br /> Since our stand in substitute story teller is so heavy handed with the combat i'm looking for a build that is somewhere in the middle, keep in mind that i've also never made a werewolf before.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically something that might make me stand out despite the fact that i'm a beginner. As far as werewolf stuff we only have the 1e Werewolf the Forsaken core book, but we also possess Armory, Armory Reloaded, Midnight Roads, Reliquary, Tales from the 13th Precinct and of course the 1e NWOD core book. We are allowed to buy any merits from any of those books with EXP or at character creation as long as we meet the perquisites and any of the equipment in those books as long as we have the appropriate amount of dots in resources.<br /> <br /> Synergies aren't necessary but they are a plus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T17:03:53-07:00","id":942325,"title":"","content":"Okay. In first edition I was really focused on spirit stuff and Auspices other than Ithaeur didn't interest me.<br /> <br /> However there's a great resource that can help you with this. <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Gifts_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">WoDCodex.</a> You should be able to skim over the Gifts available via Auspice and choose from there. Rahu and Irraka tend to be the most combat-oriented, with Rahu being more about 'warriors' and Irraka being more of the 'silent assassin.'<br /> <br /> I usually advise my players to develop a character they want to play and work mechanics from there. You can learn extra Gifts later, but if you don't like your character why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:29:24-07:00","id":942371,"title":"","content":"A big part of it is mainly experience and learning more about how each character type works, as i said i've never made a werewolf before and wanted to try it out at least once.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the link<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}